## 1. Introduction
In recent times, with the continuous consumption of non-renewable fossil sources such as coal, oil, and natural gas, pursuing innovative renewable energy techniques to address critical energy issues has become particularly significant. Newly developed, emerging electrochemical energy storage and conversion systems, including metal-ion/air batteries (where "metal" can be typically lithium, sodium, potassium, magnesium, aluminum, or zinc), supercapacitors, fuel cells, and solar cells, have attracted increasing attention and achieved encouraging success. Even though there are different
